  <div id="sutta">
  
                <h3 id="AN6.91" class="h1">Incapable<br/>
                  Abhabba Sutta  (AN 6:91)</h3><!--end suttahead-->
<p>“Monks, a person consummate in view<span class="fn"><a href="#an6.91note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--> is incapable of giving rise to six things. Which six? Self-identity view, doubt, grasping at habits &amp; practices, passion that would lead to a lower realm, anger that would lead to a lower realm, delusion that would lead to a lower realm. </p>
<p>“A person consummate in view is incapable of giving rise to these six things.”</p>
                <div class="note">
                  <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
<p id="an6.91note01">1. Consummate in view, <em>diṭṭhi-sampanna,</em> is an epithet for a person who has attained stream-entry.</p>
                </div><!--end notes-->
<p class="seealso">See also: <a href="AN3_87.html" class="sutta-ref">AN 3:87–88</a></p>


      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
